      "content": "The dimly lit, grease-stained alleyway cast a dull, yellow light over the writhing bodies. Dave's sneer cut deeper than his spats, \"You thinking you're King of Town, huh, Tiger? You better keep moving, or I'll see if you can't work it out with the wind in your eyes.\" Victor slammed his pack down, his knuckles cracking like rusty hinges, \"And how do you expect me to look like a damn nun, Black Snake, with my hands tied in the muck?\"\n\nTheir eyes—steely, cold as iron—locked, each calculating their next maneuver. Dave's lips thinned, revealing sharp, jagged teeth, as he gauged Victor's stance, every tell, every movement. Victor's broad shoulders rolled back and forth, muscles taut with anger, every sinew coiled, ready to spring. This was what they were doing now—jousting with bare fists and desperate survival, their slicked-down hair plastered to their foreheads, unkempt as if they'd just waded through the trash behind the whorehouses and seedy dives. \n\nThe tension made the air dense, charged like the atmosphere before lightning strikes. Their worn-down bodies—the testament to",
